Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was improper memory management resulting in resource leaks. In the function `libxlDomainMigrationPrepareTunnel3`, the variable `@mig` was not being set to `NULL` after being assigned, leading to potential memory leaks if an error occurred and the code exited before `@mig` was freed. Additionally, in the `libxlMigrationStartTunnel` function, the newly allocated memory for `@tc` was not being correctly saved into the provided pointer `@tnl`, which also resulted in a memory leak because the allocated resource could not be freed later. The patch addressed these issues by ensuring that memory resources are properly freed on error paths and that allocated memory is correctly referenced.
